OL,3,AAncient bridge hidden under reservoir
OL,4,Ais revealed
OL,5,
OL,6,FMonths of dry weather and prolonged
OL,7,Fheat have revealed a bridge dating back
OL,8,Fto the Victorian times that had been
OL,9,Fsubmerged during the creation of a
OL,10,Freservoir.
OL,12,FThe ancient stone Bessom Bridge flooded
OL,13,Fnearly 50 years ago when Wimbleball
OL,14,FReservoir was created at Exmoor
OL,15,FNational Park in Somerset. It was later
OL,16,Freplaced by a new bridge.
OL,18,FIn the summer, the Environment Agency
OL,19,Fdeclared that Wimbleball was one of the
OL,20,Ftop three lowest reservoirs in the
OL,21,Fcountry after levels were recorded as
OL,22,F"exceptionally low".
OL,23,APub: 03-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
